F-distribution. For non-iid errors (heteroskedastic, clustered, etc.),
a Chi-squared asymptotic distribution is used.

When \code{ci = TRUE} (or by default for iid with single endo var and no fixed effects),:
\itemize{
\item For iid errors with a single endogenous variable and no fixed effects, an exact closed-form
AR confidence interval is computed using the quadratic formula.
\item For non-iid errors with a single endogenous variable, the CI is computed by numerically inverting the AR test.
}
